# EXPECTATION FOR LANE RUN 21 — derived and committed ALONE, BEFORE the run (D0A-R21-07).
#
# Target commit: 9f6b9db. §4b's retention change was committed one commit earlier (9f6b9db) so
# this prediction is about the instrument that will actually run.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE DERIVATION
# =========================================================================================
#
# Run 20 measured root 221 / 6 / 227 at fc22117. TWO test identities added since, none removed
# (enumerated from the diff with `fn [a-z0-9_]+` — the digit-excluding form that hid the
# assembly test before run 20 is not repeated):
#
#   control_verdicts_require_provenance_and_liveness_before_naming_a_cause | b1_integration | NONE
#   proc_records_carry_provenance_and_state_for_a_real_child               | b1_integration | NONE
#
# Both ungated — verified by grep of the 25 lines after each `fn`, per the procedure's "never
# from memory" clause. Both are deliberately root-free: they exist because the control's three
# verdicts shipped UNEXECUTED inside a root-gated assertion, and a decision procedure should not
# need a privileged lane to be tested.
#
#   EXECUTED  221 + 2 = 223
#   SKIPPED       6    =   6      (unchanged; nothing added or removed is gated)
#   reported  227 + 2 = 229       (agrees with the measured unprivileged 203/26/229)
#
# Cross-check: unprivileged went 201/26/227 -> 203/26/229, i.e. +2 executed and +0 skipped —
# the same partition of the same two tests. A root figure other than 223/6/229 falsifies one of
# these two statements, and the mismatch is the result.
#
# =========================================================================================
# WHY THIS RUN EXISTS: THE ASSEMBLY TEST HAS NOT RUN SINCE ROUND 33
# =========================================================================================
#
# Since its last root execution the observer was REBUILT (provenance + liveness gating),
# `classify_control` was extracted, the probe was rewired to collect typed per-iteration
# evidence, and both outcome tables were rewritten. Meanwhile D0A-R28-02's closure rests on
# `killed == false` from that test. **The closure currently rests on a run that predates every
# change made to the thing producing it** — which is the same condition (compiled, not
# executed) one layer up from the one round 34 fixed.
#
# PART A — the standard 17-target lane, built WITHOUT the feature. Count evidence, comparable
# to run 20. Does NOT execute the assembly test.
# PART B — a SEPARATE root run of the assembly test WITH `--features insecure-test-seams`.
# Part B contributes nothing to the counts above and must not be folded into them.
#
# =========================================================================================
# WHAT A CONTROL FAILURE WOULD NOW MEAN — the verdicts are REACHABLE for the first time
# =========================================================================================
#
# In round 33 these were compiled branches. `classify_control` now computes one from evidence,
# and each says something different about whether the closure holds:
#
# 1. CONTROL PASSES (`Reached`). The scanner saw a VERIFIED, LIVE child of this daemon inside
#    its group. The supplementary scan is meaningful for this run. The §4 closure
#    (`killed == false` against a stubborn AI) is unaffected either way — it does not depend
#    on the scan.
#
# 2. `Topology`. A verified live child ran OUTSIDE the daemon's process group. **This is a
#    finding about the assembly**, and it would mean the pre-intervention scan has never been
#    able to see what it was assumed to see — the supplementary evidence in D0A-R28-02's row
#    comes out, and the row keeps only `killed == false` and the daemon's self-report. It would
#    NOT withdraw the §4 closure, because boundedness is observed independently of the scan.
#    Being able to state that separation in advance is the benefit of last round's rewrite.
#
# 3. `Scan`. A verified live child was inside the group across an overlapping window and the
#    scanner still missed it. **A defect in the control**, not evidence about the daemon — and
#    this time that is a computed verdict gated on provenance and liveness, not the rule that
#    sent every ambiguous case to this answer (D0A-R34-01/02).
#
# 4. `Unresolved`. Identity or liveness is unestablished — a namesake, a corpse, or a single
#    snapshot with no overlapping window. **Report no cause.** This is a real outcome; it is the
#    one the round-33 code could not produce, and producing it is success, not a failure to
#    diagnose.
#
# A fifth possibility is not a control failure: the control passes and
# `survivors_before_guard` is NON-EMPTY. That voids the run as evidence about the daemon and is
# caught by the assertion that already runs first.
#
# I do not know which will occur. Naming them first is what stops the one that does from
# reading as the one that was expected.
#
# =========================================================================================
# §4b's INPUTS ARE RETAINED THIS RUN — the first time the fix is applied rather than promised
# =========================================================================================
#
# Run 20's membership stands on the operator's report because both comparison inputs lived in
# /tmp and were gone when the reviewer went to check. §4b now writes
# `scratch/lane-run-21/{root-identities.txt,unpriv-identities.txt,membership.txt}` plus the
# producer transcript, and they are committed with the run record. **If those files are not in
# the commit, the membership claim for run 21 is worth exactly what run 20's was.**
EXPECTED_EXECUTED=223
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=6
EXPECTED_REPORTED=229
